	(text "NOTES\nAs-built port of the original DipTrace board (rev 0.1a, gerbers of July 2020).\nThe netlist matches the copper that was fabricated, including three open\nissues on the +5V rail:\n1. +5V_FILT (FB3 / C9 output) reaches J14 pin 11 only. The +5V bus (every\n   other header 5V pin and tip jack J8) starts at J14 pin 12. No copper joins\n   them: a shunt or solder bridge across J14 pins 11-12 powers the bus.\n2. C7 and C8 negative pins sit on their own unrouted net (C7C8_NEG), not GND,\n   so those two capacitors are out of circuit.\n3. J15 pin 4 and J8 pin 1 connect to nothing: 5V never reaches the terminal\n   block.\nNet names: *_IN before the PTC fuse, *_FUSED after it, plain rail name after\nthe ferrite bead. Capacitor values follow the BOM (the DipTrace layout marked\nall nine as 47uF)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.32 142.24 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "7a3bcaea-8267-546b-b4aa-ed32a2aca18d"))
	(sheet_instances (path "/" (page "1")))
	(embedded_fonts no)
)
